+
+## Coupled-status ownership
+
+The native `coupled-status --run-dir PATH` command owns no persistent state. It reads the version-1 `iterations.json` manifest and durable `state/tui-work.json` ledgers produced by the coupled-run writer, then emits a read-only summary. Request counts come from ledger `requests`: wire usage counts every request, while task usage counts `charge=task` and treats an omitted charge as the native task default. An interrupted ledger that is absent is reported as unknown rather than zero; declared limits remain known. The summary records native completion and stop state only and is not an independent verification or promotion decision.
